AUDIO: 'and tonight\'s two repos are exactly those parts. Part one, own the locomotive. That\'s open code, the agent itself, free, yours, model agnostic. Part two,'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'own the junction. That\'s Omni root, the routing layer that decides, request by request, which of 268 providers pulls your train. Own both, and no single company can stop'

[02:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you mid-journey. Let\'s meet the locomotive first. Open code calls itself simply the open-source coding agent. It started at SST, and now lives under Anomaly.'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '187,000 GitHub stars as of this week, MIT licensed. Moving absurdly fast, about 10 releases in the first half of July alone, and version 1.18 just completed a full'

