[13:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'part one, the gateway tax. This is the technical price of putting anything between your agent and the model. And almost nobody tells you about it. The big one is tool calling.'

[13:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'An agent isn\'t chatting. It\'s issuing tool calls. Read this file, run this test. Route those through the wrong provider and they quietly degrade. A Hacker News user, Solar Craft,'

[14:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'described running Kimi through a router in Open Code. Within a few turns, it would run off and mess something up. Terrible instruction following. On Omni Roots\' own tracker, a user'

[14:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'called Paolo La Lap, connected one of the Web Cookie providers, the ones that pretend a chat website is an API, and found his agent could not read his code base at all. The maintainer\'s answer was honest.'

[14:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Web Cookie providers can\'t do real tool calling. Some ignore tool definitions entirely. So, burn this in. For agent work, free tiers of real APIs, never the Web Cookie routes.'

[14:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Second, silent downgrades. One user, I 100 toes, selected maximum reasoning effort and caught the gateway logging it as medium. His fix was encoding the effort straight'

[14:53] [scene:talk]
